Voting Unit (Unit B):
(Wardrobe Supervisors)





In the event a majority of the valid votes case by the wardrobe supervisors are for representation by the Petitioner, the following will constitute an appropriate collective-bargaining unit;

Included:  All full-time and regular part-time costume shop assistant, sticher, crafts artisan, cutter/draper, tailor, milliner, wig crafts and wig master employees employed by the Employer at its Issaquah, Washington location, and all full-time and regular part-time wardrobe supervisors employed by the Employer at its Everett and Issaquah, Washington locations; 

Excluded:   All other employees, guards and supervisors as defined in the Act.

